# Marks, memory and timing — 2026-11-14
#
# A reader on X said Spw is not a programming language. The owner asked to reflect on the syntax, on referencing and dereferencing, on functional projection, on the practical effects of $substrate against substrate$ and of $%[subject.item] against $#[subject.item], [subject.item]#$ and [subject.item]%$, with spw.quest and factshift.center in view, and asked that operators behave so their combinations carry an author's intent about memory and timing. Three agents studied spw.quest, factshift.center, and the workbench's field theory against its runtime; their reports follow the synthesis, verbatim. Nothing here changes a parser, a runtime or a host.

#>journal_2026_11_14_marks_memory_timing
#:cache #!observation
#:layer #!semantics

^["entry"]{
 date: "2026-11-14"
 kind: #observation
 base: "this repo at 1f87112f; spwashi.com read in place at its main; no consumer written"
 method: "programs run through runSpw and interpretSeed; forms printed as parse trees; lexer token censuses over three corpora; three read only agents with file and line citations, each probe run inline"
 limits: "nothing was rendered or heard; the agents' citations were spot checked (the label and value split, the recursion's parse, the set ONF, the guide's Runtime lines, factshift's loader rule), not all re-read"
 cards: [~"../../../.agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw#wonder_trial_evaluation_core", ~"../../../.agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw#wonder_trial_reference_position"]
}

^["measured"]{
 # What the workbench does today, run rather than read.
 runtime: "no environment: *x{5} then @x writes 5 to the focus register and observes x as null; =total[3] writes a register named 3; a record evaluates to its last value, a set to nothing; .{ a = 1, b = 2 } / a evaluates to the string a; ?[true]{ yes } evaluates to true"
 why_names_fail: "normalizeToONF files the word of *x{5} under frames.label and the interpreter reads frames.value (interpreter.ts frameString), so the name never reaches the register bank"
 onf_losses: "ONF of #[1, 2, 3] keeps value 1 and armCount 3 and drops 2 and 3; the parser's tree keeps every member, so an evaluator walks the tree"
 computes_today: "the quantity sheet (acyclic dataflow over @names), settings lines against a vocabulary, selectors, and lowerings to CSS, GPU buffers, audio and WGSL; rewrite by example is a file tool, not an evaluator"
 parses_already: "@sum: ?match[_]{ [] => 0, [@h, ...@t] => @t / @sum + @h } and @total: #[1, 2, 3] / @sum parse with no error or warning; a throwaway walk of the tree returned 6"
 misreads: "@double[x = 4]/out floats its frame onto the whole expression and splits x = 4 in three; @x*2 reads * as the crystallize mark; ?[@n < 2] degrades its line to prose; *@side is two statements; no minus sign lexes"
}

^["dollar_variants"]{
 # Each form as the parser, the runtime, the editor and the corpus meet it.
 dollar_word: "$substrate is one operation labelled substrate; the runtime returns the focus register's meta and drops the label; painted as a variable; said substrate substrate; written 78 times here, 139 in the story consumer, 69 on the site; every spw.quest room takes it"
 word_dollar: "substrate$ is two statements; said as the raw word, its mark unnamed; written nowhere; refused by every spw.quest room; inside a JavaScript template literal runway${months, team} is an interpolation that throws at load; factshift's canvas reads marks by first character, so it acts on no mark"
 dollar_percent: "$%[subject.item] is a bare $ then %[subject.item]; the runtime makes a register named subject.item; the highlighter paints $%[ as one keyword; said substrate measure mode subject.item; written 1,205 here, 32 in the story consumer, 476 on the site; read by six text patterns, never from the tree"
 dollar_hash: "$#[subject.item] is a bare $ then #[subject.item], a resonance register; said substrate vibration mode subject.item; written nowhere"
 postfix_frames: "[subject.item]#$ and [subject.item]%$ are three statements each; said mode subject.item, vibration substrate and mode subject.item, measure substrate; written nowhere; a trailing $ before a word captures it as a modifier ([a.b]#$ x)"
 hash_first: "#$ at a line start parses as one # whose payload is the rest of the line as prose, and factshift's loader cuts it as a comment"
 two_meanings: "spw.quest teaches $%[ ] as what a question would measure or the answers it chooses among; $#[ ] could say the answer set, a set with no scale, leaving $%[ ] for what is measured, so the form would say which"
}

^["combinations"]{
 # How marks written side by side are read, and how often they are written.
 composed_today: "only the particles compose: #! 15,236, #: 14,139, #> 12,116 across three corpora, one token each with a defined meaning"
 split_today: "$% 1,722, $^ 277, =@ 238, =~ 150, =# 94, $# 46 are written and none composes; the parser splits each run, factshift's canvas obeys the first mark, a mark joint turn overwrites the whole run"
 convergence: "three agents, briefed apart, read a run the same way: the outer or left mark says when or the stance, the inner or right mark says what happens to memory; nearest binds tightest, as the particle lattice already orders stance, plane and aim"
 tilde_star: "~*x a commit that waits for its first read, a lazy cell memoized when read; *~x a promise committed now, an option kept open on purpose; checkable as writes before first read, 0 against 1"
 bang_tilde: "!~x actualizes what was primed now; ~!x primes an act held for later or a condition, as factshift's pending ties and spw.quest's primed turn already behave"
 dollar_percent_pair: "$%x the address of a measurement on x, its value unread; %$x a measure of the store itself: writes, age, frequency, or the cost spw.quest's algorithms file writes as <log_n>"
 dollar_hash_pair: "$#x the address of a lens over x, or a fact kept under a name; #$x a set of addresses or the name of a store, unwritable while # opens a heading"
 readable_now: "operator token spans tell ~*x from ~ *x, so a reader can see a run without a grammar change"
}

^["found"]{
 # Defects and gaps met on the way; each belongs to the repository named.
 workbench_names: "the label and value split above: the cheapest real fix in the runtime, and a behaviour change for every bound name"
 workbench_unwired: "nothing calls Substrate.bind, so an event has no handler; nothing calls field.ts, so the field primitives have no sites"
 quest_overclaims: "spw.quest prints under Runtime that ~ defers evaluation as a thunk until an observer demands it and that $ materializes memory layout, latency bounds and resource footprints (src/guide.js 8 and 19, index.js 347); the runtime does neither, and an engineer will check"
 quest_glosses: "$ is time, money, machines in the guide and time, money, memory, attention in the answer form"
 factshift_loader: "src/js/modes/spw/spw-tree.ts cuts a # at a line start or after a space as a comment unless > : [ { ( or @ follows, so #:layer #!pragmatics loads as #:layer and #! focus tags are lost wherever they follow a space"
 factshift_pin: "factshift runs the workbench pinned at fffab72 from 2026-03-12 and reads with the 2026.11.07-pre.1 reader"
 factshift_scenes: "the director plays a scene's events, but nothing calls registerScene"
}

^["readings"]{
 # Open, as the trial cards hold them; not decisions.
 core: "total dataflow, the sheet's rule made general over the parser's tree: a binding is a cell with its inputs, a write relights its dependents, recursion only by structure over a finite set, so every program ends"
 lazy: "records and references as Jsonnet and Nix: fields forced on demand, a demand trace to draw, programs that may not end"
 effects: "operators as requests a host handles, the queue drawn; a layer over a core, not a core"
 field: "spw.quest's floor and factshift's canvas already draw potential dashed or faint and consequence as heat; a field reads a program's dependency graph, it does not replace one"
 smallest_slice: "an evaluator that walks the tree in about 530 new lines in five new runtime files (cells, the walk, a field view, tests, a CLI card), changing no existing file and exporting nothing until a release names it; first program the fold above, first combination ~*x against *~x"
}

# ── spw.quest, by an agent reading workers/spw-quest ─────────────

#>quest_field_report
#:report #!spw_quest #!dollar
*method = `read src; ran each room's own reader on the variants and the mark pairs from stdin; parser builds 2026.10.13, 2026.11.13 and the site bundle at 27fa1e3d16ab agree on every line probed; two probe scripts sit in this session's scratchpad, probe.mjs and reads.mjs, and nothing else was written`
*paths = `bare names are workers/spw-quest/src; expression-query.js is spwashi.com public/js/semantic; sheet.ts, field.ts, interpreter.ts, register-bank.ts, substrate.ts and hot-session.ts are in the workbench packages`

^"today"{
  reads = `only parse is imported, from the site bundle spw-workbench-reader.js built from workbench 0.3.0 at 27fa1e3d16ab (reader.js:4, file-reader.js:5, physics.js:26, build.js:4)`
  page_builds = `the guide's editor reads with the pinned /parser/2026.10.13/reader.min.js (index.js:425, shell-pin.js:14); /learn, /build and /physics read with /parser.js (reader.js:259, file-reader.js:984, physics.js:1120)`
  slot_reader = `a second reader, regex over text, gives subject, mode, body, scene and concept to the shelf, pivot, card and constructs (expression-query.js:95, specimen-reading.js:31)`
  checks = [`Learn panels run named checks over the AST and render Passes or Not yet (reader.js:60, 155)`, `file checks are held equal to the site's spw-genre-checks.js (test/genre.test.mjs:17)`]
  file_reading = `the file reader collects names, tags, fields, links, dated entries, questions with probes, notes, frames, mark counts and checks (file-reader.js:73)`
  floor = `/physics lays one line out as bodies inside bodies on springs, one law per mark (physics.js:57, 91, 226)`
  shelf = [`the shelf's specimens arrive read when carried (specimen-reading.js:1, constructs.js:26)`, `a typed line on /card and /pivot is read per request (answer.js:137, pivot.js:192)`]
  runtime = `nothing evaluates: no file in src imports runSpw; workbench.min.js with runSpw, createHotSession, readQuantitySheet and diffuseField is served at /parser/2026.11.13/ only as a described download (parser-releases.js:204, 212)`
  runtime_claim = `the guide prints a Runtime line per mark and calls it what the reader does today (index.js:347, 387); $ claims memory layout, latency bounds and resource footprints (guide.js:19) where interpreter.ts:256 returns a register's descriptor, provenance, lenses and valence (register-bank.ts:502)`
  runtime_claim_potential = `~ claims a thunk kept until an observer demands it (guide.js:8); interpreter.ts:293 wraps its argument as deferred, and ! returns its argument rather than forcing one (interpreter.ts:285)`
  two_glosses = `$ is time, money, machines on the guide (guide.js:19) and time, money, memory, attention in the answer form (answer.js:37); test/answer.test.mjs:24 holds only sigil and name equal`
  memory = `four localStorage keys, all set by src and none by workers/lib or the peer scripts, per device and never sent: spw.quest.note/1, spw.quest.hand/1, spw.quest.walk/1, spw.quest.display/1 (note.js:10, file-reader.js:715, walk.js:18, display.js:10)`
  memory_more = `the shell caches the guide and the pinned reader (assets/sw.js:6); the address carries ?line, ?share, ?example, ?at and #spw64 (physics.js:628, index.js:719, walk.js:179); wrangler.jsonc binds only ASSETS, so there is no server store`
  names = [`no name is looked up to a value: a field shows its shape (file-reader.js:92)`, `resolution is only @handle paths between files and landing on a line by name (file-reader.js:158, 438)`, `and /physics sight lines matched by word inside one line (physics.js:216)`]
  consequence = `an edit reparses the whole file once per frame, repaints, redraws the reading and the hand, then keeps the note (file-reader.js:756, 773, 782)`
  consequence_effect = `the one effect beyond reading: a pattern field and a theme field set the editor's theme (file-reader.js:229, 761; examples.js:301)`
  consequence_preview = `the hand primes a turn on a copy and lists what would read differently before Write, with Put it back after (file-reader.js:487, 552, 744)`
  consequence_floor = `/physics keeps touch, visitor and keep apart; only keep changes bytes, with undo and a byte count (physics.js:2, 413, 830, 853)`
  potential = `~ keeps options open (guide.js:8) and drifts on the floor (physics.js:61); the walk writes unopened rooms as ~room (walk.js:107)`
  potential_drawn = `the unwritten is dashed: the landing ghost, the amber visitor the line does not write, a warm body while it moves (physics.js:948, 946, 480, 934)`
  potential_gap = `a ? has no answer slot: on experiment.spw the reading keeps the question and its probe, and $%[ring.reads, pill.reads, neither] adds only one $ and one % to the mark counts (examples.js:117, file-reader.js:178)`
  algorithms_now = `algorithms.spw names binary search, merge sort, bfs, dfs, a window and memo as paths of marked steps, and nothing runs them (examples.js:559); it says cost rides in the scene but writes it in the concept brace, <log_n> (examples.js:552, 564)`
}

^"references"{
  at = [`@name: with a path is a handle the reading turns into a way to that file (file-reader.js:314)`, `viewer@subject is perspective, settled (constructs.js:270)`, `@ before a word is a Reference node (reader.js:67)`, `nowhere does @ yield a value`]
  slash = `no / projection is taught: a search of examples, constructs, steps, guide, answer and starters for a spaced slash or a slash after a brace found none; / sits only inside quoted paths, and the card path test refuses a / inside braces (answer.js:183)`
  dot = `software.art.practice is one word to the parser and three parts to the search (constructs.js:272); . in front is ground and settles on the floor (physics.js:58)`
}

^"dollar_variants"{
  taught = `prefix only: $runway{months, team} (guide.js:19), $ground[material]{grain.tooth} pressed on the substrate card (constructs.js:62), source = $orders[csv]{id, customer, qty, price} (examples.js:403); /pivot offers $ in front (pivot.js:21)`
  taught_list = `$%[...] is a measure list, what a question would measure or the answers it chooses among, and its card says the form does not say which (constructs.js:96); a text test finds it, not the parser`
  taught_postfix = `never written; the act panel says door~ reads as a door then a thought with nothing to hold, and leaves binding open (steps.js:29)`
  floor = `$ has no law on the floor and a $ visitor is not worn (physics.js:57, test/physics.test.mjs:188)`
  prefix_substrate = `every room takes it: the reading marks orders as substrate, /build splits mark from word (build.js:106), /card routes $substrate<card> (answer.js:183), the act panel passes (reader.js:65), /physics takes $runway{months, team}`
  postfix_substrate = `the act panel fails with No mark in front of a word yet; /build, /card and /physics refuse runway${months, team}, the floor because it finds two expressions (physics.js:102); the reading's marked words drop it`
  postfix_gain = `it would give the act panel's open question about door~ one tested answer (steps.js:29), and reads like a unit after a number`
  postfix_disagree = `the slot reader keeps substrate$ as one subject while the parser reads two statements, a gap of the kind the bench tracks (bench.js:12)`
  postfix_template = `every example sits in a JS template literal (examples.js:49), where runway${months, team} is an interpolation that throws at load unless escaped; prefix $runway{ is safe there`
  shell = `in a double-quoted shell string $runway expands and runway${ is a bad substitution, so either form needs single quotes in a shell`
  dollar_measure = `$%[subject.item] is two statements, a bare $ then %[subject.item]; the slot reader calls $% a word with mode subject.item, so a shelf line would count $ in front and % inside a word (constructs.js:37); the measure-list test matches`
  dollar_set = `$#[subject.item] is two statements too; the measure-list test misses and the set test hits (constructs.js:91, 96), and the reading moves one count from % to #`
  dollar_set_gain = `$#[...] could say the answers chosen among, a set with no order, leaving $%[...] for what is measured: the form would then say which`
  postfix_set = `[subject.item]#$ is a frame, a bare # and a bare $; the slot reader keeps only the mode and marks the line partial; the reading lists no frame, since it wants an operation that holds one (file-reader.js:174)`
  postfix_capture = `[a.b]#$ x hands x to $ as a modifier, so a trailing mark binds forward to whatever follows on the line`
  postfix_measure = `[subject.item]%$ reads alike, % then $; the measure-list test misses; it would read left to right as list, how measured, what it runs on`
  hash_first = `at a line start #$ is no pair: #$runway and #$[subject.item] parse as one # whose payload is the rest of the line as prose, while $#runway is two operations`
}

^"readings"{
  sheet = .{
    model = `the file is a sheet of named terms; a cell holds its written span, an expression with @name refs, a value or a problem, its dependencies and the beat it last changed`
    step = `readQuantitySheet already resolves on demand, reports unknown_reference and cycle as problems, and reads on top of a base sheet (sheet.ts:232)`
    edit = `re-read, diff the values against the last read, and light the dependents that changed, as means() already diffs two readings (file-reader.js:487)`
    potential = `a referenced but unwritten term is a dashed cell; a ?[...] holding $%[a, b] is a cell whose value waits for its probe`
    dollar = `$name names the base sheet a sheet is read on, what the computation runs on`
    renders = `a strip of cells under the editor, @refs drawn as sight lines, each cell a handle the hand can hold and turn`
    costs = [`acyclic by design, so no recursion and no loop`, `numbers with units only`, `only terms led by % count at workbench head, a change (4fdccc16) made after the 2026.11.13 cut`, `workbench.min.js is 505 KB against the 88 KB pinned reader (shell-pin.js:15) unless the sheet is carried alone`]
  }
  machine = .{
    model = `an environment of bindings, name to value, provenance and beat, beside the runtime's register bank and its event log (substrate.ts:91)`
    step = `small steps, one register event each; =name{v} binds, @name reads, . and / project from a record`
    edit = `rerun from the top with fuel and diff the two traces; the first event that differs is the consequence`
    potential = `~x{...} stays a deferred card until ! or a tap forces it; a ? whose condition is unknown is drawn as two open branches`
    dollar = `$name opens a value's provenance, where it came from, which is what interpreter.ts:256 already returns`
    renders = `the editor with the current node lit by the CSS highlights the hand uses (file-reader.js:688), a register table, and a scrubber over beats`
    costs = [`needs the environment the runtime lacks`, `settles @ as reads where a trial is open`, `makes the Runtime column true by making Spw conventional`, `needs a step cap on a phone`]
  }
  field = .{
    model = `memory is amplitude per site (field.ts:15); sites are a file's names and bodies, edges its ~> joins, @refs and nesting`
    step = `a beat is decayField then diffuseField over the edges (field.ts:56, 75), each mark a law as the floor already has it (physics.js:57)`
    edit = `a write or a touch injects amplitude at one site; the consequence is how far and how fast it spreads, as a touch already warms a body and by the share its insides (physics.js:324)`
    potential = `declared sites at zero, ~ bodies and unanswered ?, drawn dashed until something reaches them`
    dollar = `$ names the carrier and its capacity (field.ts:18, 26), the time, money or attention a field spends`
    renders = `the /physics floor with heat, a beat button, and the measures table kept checkable by hand (physics.js:491)`
    costs = [`continuous and approximate, so a map or a fold has no exact answer`, `engineers read a simulation, not a program`, `the numbers are a feel the creator sets (physics.js:19)`]
  }
}

^"algorithms"{
  map = `!map[double]{@xs} as input and output columns joined by lines, where an edit to one member relights one output; the machine does it directly, the sheet needs a term per member, the field only blurs it`
  fold = `%sum{total} as an accumulator strip, one cell per step under a scrubber; an edit at step k relights k onward, a visible suffix`
  recursion = `memo = path{?seen{subproblem}; !solve; #keep{answer}} (examples.js:569) as a call tree of bodies inside bodies; unexpanded calls are dashed ~ bodies a tap forces; #keep turns repeats into sight lines; the floor stops at depth 3 (physics.js:55)`
  search = `bfs = path{=queue{start}; ~visit{edges}; #seen{node}} (examples.js:566) on a graph already in hand, the 26 example files and their @links (file-reader.js:604); frontier dashed ~, seen solid #, current !, one hop a step; it answers the file's own probe, count hops from Home (examples.js:571)`
}

^"combinatorics"{
  today_rule = `adjacent marks do not compose: the inner mark takes the word or the frame and the outer stands alone; ~*draft is a bare ~ then *draft; %$[x] gives the frame to $ and $%[x] gives it to %`
  today_credit = [`the reading credits only the inner mark`, `/pivot strips the whole run when it turns a mark (pivot.js:204)`, `/build takes one mark (build.js:106)`, `the balloon reads only the first token (reader.js:123)`]
  fused = `the lexer already fuses #>, #:, #!, ~# and ~> into single tokens (guide.js:31, constructs.js:80, 95), the shape a pair would take`
  nested = `the floor's share is the one composition taught: a body inside a marked body feels that law alike, softer or faint (physics.js:10, 145), composition by nesting, not adjacency`
  want_memory = [`kept across visits: the note, the walk, the display, and the word of the line last held (file-reader.js:715)`, `kept for a page: the undo stack, the held part and the primed turn (physics.js:533, file-reader.js:904)`, `forgotten at once: a touch comes home and a visitor leaves unless kept (physics.js:3)`]
  want_timing = [`now: each frame's reparse (file-reader.js:782)`, `each beat: the floor's 1/60 s step, and a body that cools after 12 calm steps (physics.js:80, 310)`, `on change: the input listener (file-reader.js:792)`, `until: settle to rest (physics.js:317)`, `later: dated entries (file-reader.js:48)`]
  order = `one reading: the outer mark says when or how long and the inner says what; adjacency for time, nesting for scope`
  tilde_star = `~*draft is a value not yet kept, the hand's primed turn and the visitor before keep; *~draft is an option kept open on purpose, like the walk's ~room lines that persist`
  bang_tilde = `!~draft forces the maybe now, the floor's keep; ~!draft is an act held for later or for a condition, which a !probe inside a ? already is`
  dollar_pct = `$%x measures on a substrate, what a question would measure; %$x measures the substrate itself, the cost algorithms.spw now writes as <log_n>`
  dollar_hash = `$#x names a member held on a substrate; #$x is unavailable without a lexer change, since # at a line start takes the rest of the line as prose`
  dollar_store = `$ could name where a memory lives, among the four stores spw.quest has: the device, the address, the page session and the shell cache; *$device would read as a value kept on this device`
  until = `until a condition can be ?ready ~> !ship, the path the quest already teaches (constructs.js:80), so it needs no new pair`
  each_beat = `each beat has no mark yet; a [beat] mode or %beat{decay} could say it, and the workbench keeps beat tiers for its caches (hot-session.ts:82)`
  contradicts = `pairs contradict the act panel's one mark in front of a word (steps.js:26) and the guide's twelve single sigils; pivot, /build, the balloon and the reading's credit would each need a mark run`
  extends = `pairs extend the act panel's ~door, ?door, !door, the walk's mixed marks and the floor's composed laws`
}

?["Is $ what a computation runs on, or the cell a value lives in?"]{
  ~#readings: [`sheet: the base sheet`, `machine: a value's provenance`, `field: the carrier and its capacity`, `memory: the store a value is kept in`]
  !probe{ "write one fold three ways in pipeline.spw, read each in the guide's editor, and count which rooms still take it" }
}
?["Do adjacent marks compose by order, or does composition stay with nesting?"]{
  ~#readings: [`order: the outer mark is when, the inner is what`, `fusion: a lexer pair like ~> or #>`, `nesting: the floor's share`]
}

# ── factshift.center, by an agent reading workers/factshift-center ─

#>factshift_field_report
^"scope"{
  host = `air/spwashi.com/workers/factshift-center, app checkout 1a4157a, read only; js/ and ts/ paths are under app/src, .spw/ paths under app, src/index.js and wrangler.jsonc are the worker's, packages/ is spw-workbench`
  worker = `no KV, no server state: src/index.js:13 only serves env.ASSETS and sends www to the apex; wrangler.jsonc binds ASSETS alone`
  prior_dpad = `d-pad levels step a tool's menu, cards and controls (js/ui/focal-point.ts:387)`
  prior_containers = `a container a hand moved or resized keeps its place by word and slot (region-overrides.ts:1, body-gestures.ts)`
  prior_atlas = `the atlas is app/.spw, a state and feature atlas (.spw/state/index.spw:1, commit 427d70d)`
  prior_scoping = `atlas modifier scoping not found under that name; nearest are body laws scoped to their own members (local-forces.ts:1) and keyboard modifiers said to mirror operator tenses (js/init/hotkeys/keystrokes.ts:95)`
}
^"today"{
  reads = [
    `slot reader: workbench bundle 2026.11.07-pre.1 (js/vendor/spw-reader/release.json), readLine and writeLine via line-slots.ts:18, line-paint.ts:18, file-map.ts:22`,
    `form reader: line-forms.ts sorts a statement into binding, prose, scalar, set, path, entry, reference, header or tags before the slot reader sees it (line-forms.ts:46)`,
    `runtime: workbench submodule pinned at fffab72, aliased in vite.config.js; every run calls collectPrecipitates (ts/spw/workbench-adapter.ts:37)`,
    `legacy parser vendor/spw/parser/parse.mjs is live only in the heading (js/ui/h1.ts:9); its mode-spw.ts:303 fallback is unreachable because isRuntimeTraceShown is constant false (mode-spw.ts:56)`
  ]
  line_to_screen = [
    `Run (js/modes/spw/mode-spw.ts:225) routes settings and superpowers by regex and commands by name (process-line.ts:16); the first Spw line is held (mode-spw.ts:255), several go to the thread (mode-spw.ts:253)`,
    `setHeldLine writes storage, title, the ?spw= address and a history entry, then projects the anatomy (held-line.ts:40, held-line.ts:43, held-line.ts:46)`,
    `projectLineAnatomy turns word, [ ] mode, { } body parts, ( ) scene and < > concept into d3 nodes, links and regions (line-anatomy.ts:1172)`,
    `the canvas is a force field: link, collide, many body charge, center, gravity wells for mass over 2, operator forces, body laws, brace pairs at k q q over d (ts/simulation/forces.ts:469, forces.ts:219, particles.ts:1)`,
    `by the constants, a top level word (r 34, line-anatomy.ts:217) has mass about 2.9 (r squared over 400, normalize.ts:34) and is a gravity well (mass over 2, forces.ts:227) while a part at r 16 is not; seats and charge act too, so the pull is not checked on screen`,
    `a node moves by the first character of its name (operator-physics.ts:30); a body moves its members by its word's first mark (local-forces.ts:44); # and $ have no law and keep the field's (local-forces.ts:21)`,
    `the runtime draws nothing on the canvas: its result goes to a summary, a steps panel and a per node card (workbench-runtime.ts:1367, workbench-steps.ts:1, runtime-card.ts:1)`
  ]
  fact_shift_model = `absent as data: nothing named fact or shift; the unit is the held line, and the nearest shift is a timed StageEvent of params and nodes (ts/stage/scene.ts:6), authored in TypeScript only`
  memory = [
    `all of it is this browser's localStorage plus the URL; the code keeps at least ten factshift keys`,
    `thread of the last 40 lines factshift.talk (spw-talk.ts:42); 8 kept lines, each a colored perspective, factshift.kept (spw-kept.ts:9)`,
    `12 word pins (identity-pins.ts:14); hand-placed containers by word and slot (region-overrides.ts:17); crawled .spw tree of 64 nodes (spw-tree.ts:53)`,
    `stage frames keyed by md5 of the heading's line (ts/stage/frame.ts:17); one history entry per concept (js/ui/concept-history.ts:45)`,
    `a node keeps its place across an edit by role and name, not id (line-anatomy.ts:1172)`,
    `the runtime remembers nothing between presses: a register bank is rebuilt from the selection on each run (ts/spw/session-context.ts:303)`
  ]
  consequence = [
    `a press leaves a receipt near the handle that expires (js/ui/handle-said.ts:10); every press is typed open, commit, cycle, toggle, close or inspect (js/ui/interaction-tree.ts:9)`,
    `a canvas edit rewrites the held line and every listener follows: title, address, thread row, operator keys (held-line.ts:49)`,
    `a tap on a marked node does its mark once: . grounds, = pins, @ centers, * grows, # saves a frame, & selects ties, % says size, $ says kind and id (js/simulation/nodes/operator-tap.ts:47)`,
    `the field's one clock is heat: a change reheats alpha, which decays to rest in about two seconds (forces.ts:484, particles.ts:1); other clocks are fixed interface timers`,
    `scheduled change lives only in TypeScript: story mode runs hardcoded delayed events (js/modes/story/mode-story.ts:136)`,
    `the director plays a scene's events after their delays (ts/stage/director.ts:48), but nothing calls registerScene (ts/stage/scene.ts:24), so scene play finds no scene`
  ]
  potential = [
    `empty slots are faint regions drawn only while a drag could fill them (line-anatomy.ts:98, line-anatomy.ts:664, js/simulation/nodes/handling/circle.ts:484)`,
    `a held tie is a pending prime or gather, shown by data-tie, written by ! or lifted into the line by ^ (link-confirm.ts:32, render/join.ts:75, link-confirm.ts:105, link-confirm.ts:131)`,
    `an operator joint primes a turn and a second press actualizes it (operator-field.ts:1, line-joints.ts:30)`,
    `what no slot reads is an unread strip (line-anatomy.ts:1123) and a rest tone in the prompt (line-paint.ts:148); an open brace gets a ghost closer (line-paint.ts:7)`,
    `a question body never folds; it closes when the line answers it (brace-folds.ts:13)`,
    `a ~ node lets half its seat go (operator-physics.ts:1); the runtime's ~ returns a deferred wrapper that only the node card names (.spw/_workbench/src/runtime/interpreter/interpreter.ts:276, runtime-card.ts:148)`,
    `Run says what it will do before the press (spw-interpret.ts:17); a map cast lights and counts its hits before it lands (js/modes/mapfilter/mode-mapfilter.ts:139)`
  ]
}
^"census"{
  own = `factshift's own: 18 files, 715 nonblank lines, the state and feature atlases from March 2026; the app never reads them`
  own_leads = `string items 274, braces 127, ~# stance keys 121 (~#role, ~#sources, ~#keys), ^"section" heads 75, @ keys 42, ~"path" refs 71, # prose headers 18`
  own_absent = `confirmed: no $, no %, no #[ ], no #> header and no / projection in the 18`
  own_at = `@ appears only as a binding key before a ~"path" value (@state_surface, @spec); never as a join or a read`
  vendored = `correction: about 237 of the 257 are the workbench corpus vendored at app/.spw/_workbench (fffab72): 787 $ outside quotes, 455 lines led by $%, 167 by $^, 45 by $#`
  crawled = `the local checkout of what the crawler can reach, spwashi.com/.spw (spw-tree.ts:558), deployed copy not checked: 763 files, about 100 thousand lines, 322 $ outside quotes, 300 of them $%[ list ], 10 $word, no word$, no postfix #$ or %$`
  runs = `mark runs outside quotes in spwashi.com/.spw: ~# 9746, #! 3984, $% 300, &? 7, $^ 6, &~ 1; none of ~* *~ !~ ~! %$ #$ $#`
  loader_cut = `the loader for files, pastes and links treats a # at line start or after a space, unless followed by > : [ { ( @, as a comment (spw-tree.ts:82, via spw-talk.ts:94)`
  loader_cost = `run on samples: #$x and #!components load as nothing, #:log #!components keeps only #:log, so the crawled corpus's #! tags (3984) are cut on load wherever they follow a space or start a line`
  stale = `atlas persistence.spw names no factshift key; the code moved on and the atlas did not`
}
^"dollar_variants"{
  method = `each form read three ways on factshift's own pins (slot reader, form reader, runtime fffab72), probed read only`
  dollar_substrate = .{ slot = `one whole word $substrate`, runtime = `one $ op labelled substrate; it materializes the focus register, named by a double quote, and drops the label (interpreter.ts:246, register-bank.ts:21)`, canvas = `no body law; a tap says kind and id; never echoes, since resonate wants word characters only (line-anatomy.ts:1146)`, verdict = `works today; matches the substrate entry in operators.ts:16` }
  substrate_dollar = .{ slot = `one whole word substrate$`, runtime = `two statements`, canvas = `markless: every dispatch reads charAt(0) and every strip is anchored at the start (operator-tap.ts:47, line-joints.ts:16)`, verdict = `breaks silently: canvas and runtime disagree on count and no mark acts` }
  dollar_pct = .{ slot = `word $% with [ ] mode subject.item`, form = `two or more items draw as a set titled $%[ ] (line-forms.ts:106, line-anatomy.ts:755)`, runtime = `$ then %[subject.item]`, verdict = `the crawled corpus's habit (300 lines); extends with no break` }
  dollar_hash = .{ slot = `word $# with mode subject.item`, runtime = `$ then #[subject.item], a resonance register`, canvas = `a front mark turn returns nothing, the bare word being empty (line-joints.ts:77)`, verdict = `reads today; rare in what the host meets` }
  postfix_hash = .{ slot = `whole false, rest #$`, runtime = `three statements`, verdict = `breaks editing, ties and casts until the slot reader learns a trailing mark` }
  postfix_hash_canvas = [
    `drawn as an unread #$ strip under the reading (line-anatomy.ts:1123)`,
    `a slot edit refuses (line-slots.ts:232)`,
    `a ^ lift replaces the whole held line with a new host body (link-confirm.ts:137)`,
    `spaced, [subject.item] #$ loads as [subject.item], the loader cutting #$ as a comment (spw-tree.ts:82)`
  ]
  postfix_pct = .{ slot = `whole false, rest %$`, canvas = `same unread strip and refusals as #$`, runtime = `three statements; % measures 1`, verdict = `same cost as postfix #$` }
  capture = `[a.b]#$ x: the pinned runtime takes x as a modifier on $ while the slot reader leaves #$ x unread, so the two disagree about x`
}
^"combinatorics"{
  needs = [
    `persist: kept lines, pins, container places, the thread; today implicit in localStorage keys, never said by the line`,
    `decay: receipts expire, heat cools, the thread drops past 40, kept lines evict the oldest past 8 (spw-kept.ts:10)`,
    `trigger on change: held line listeners (held-line.ts:23) and map previews on input`,
    `scheduled: only TypeScript story delays and an empty scene registry; no Spw line can schedule`,
    `held until a condition: a question body, a pending tie, a primed joint, a potentiated slot`
  ]
  today = [
    `canvas: the first mark wins and the rest of the run is ignored (operator-tap.ts:47, operator-physics.ts:30, local-forces.ts:44)`,
    `runtime fffab72 splits a run into separate ops: ~*x{5} is a bare ~ then *x{5}, and *~x{5} is * then ~x{5}`,
    `the mark joint writes one sigil over the whole run, so a turn erases a combination (line-joints.ts:77)`,
    `already distinct by accident: a %$ body levels its members while a $% body has no law; ~* drifts while *~ holds heavy`
  ]
  rule = `one reading consistent with the # led particles (#> anchor, #: lens, #! focus) and $%[ ]: the left mark is the carrier or stance, the right mark is what it carries`
  rule_test = `#! fits if # is the particle head and ! the focus it carries; ~# is a stance whose name is still open, so it backs the order more than a meaning`
  tense_precedent = `the keyboard already pairs , and . as potential and materialized (keystrokes.ts:95), a two key habit a mark pair could mirror`
  tilde_star = .{ reads = `~*x a value that may collapse, drawn hollow until it does; *~x a weight held loose, heavy yet unseated`, extends = `~ deferral (interpreter.ts:276) and * as mass (normalize.ts:34)` }
  dollar_pct = .{ reads = `$%[ ] a measure kept in a substrate, the crawled contract; %$x a gauge of a store: its size, age or decay`, extends = `the set form and its title (line-anatomy.ts:755)`, contradicts = `nothing in place; %$ gives % a law where $% has none` }
  dollar_hash = .{ reads = `$#x a fact kept under a name, persisting; #$x the name of a store (thread, kept, URL)`, contradicts = `a leading or spaced #$ is a comment to the loader, so #$x loads as nothing (spw-tree.ts:82)` }
  bang_tilde = .{ reads = `~!x an act held until its condition, which the tie flow already says as ~ then ! (link-confirm.ts:87, link-confirm.ts:105); !~x act now and leave the result loose`, extends = `pending ties and primed joints` }
  costs = `every combination needs run aware dispatch in three places, a joint that edits one mark of a run, and the runtime reading a run as one operator`
}
^"readings"{
  one = .{ model = `field over held lines: a fact is a node of a held, kept or thread line; a shift is the diff between two versions; weight is *, memory is the thread row's age`, evaluates = `the existing d3 tick; influence by gravity wells and the 1/d charge, decay by alpha and row age, distance by slotHash vectors from the reader bundle`, renders = `a potential contour sampled under the nodes, unfilled slots and pending ties as charged faint regions, a shift as a well moving with a trail`, costs = `answers are positions, not values; layout is not deterministic; an engineer still cannot get a number out` }
  two = .{ model = `sheet as field: facts are %name[expr] terms with @name references, from the workbench's experimental spw.quantity-sheet/1 (packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/physics/sheet.ts)`, evaluates = `an edit recomputes its dependents in topological order; unknown references and cycles are open sockets`, renders = `terms as nodes, references as ties, a changed term pulses and its dependents relight in order; distance is hops`, costs = `absent from the reader bundle's exports and from fffab72, so a bundle cut first; numbers with units only; acyclic, so no recursion; its @ means a reference while the canvas's @ is a perspective join` }
  three = .{ model = `register bank as memory: keep the runtime's bank across runs with provenance, writes, lastUsedAt and liminality local, liminal, visible, global (.spw/_workbench/src/runtime/state/types.ts:110)`, evaluates = `* writes, ~ defers, ! commits, $ materializes a register's meta and provenance as it already does (interpreter.ts:246)`, renders = `registers as wells whose mass is writes, glow is liminality and fade is time since last use; a deferred value hollow until a ! lands`, costs = `needs the runtime to gain an environment first (today *x writes the focus register); the pin is eight months behind; a kept bank makes runs order dependent` }
}
^"algorithms"{
  map = `exists in Spw: a slot cast [body]{draft ~> fact} rewrites one slot across the lines in scope, with undo (js/modes/mapfilter/slot-cast.ts:11, mode-mapfilter.ts:174)`
  filter = `exists: a selection algebra over slot asks with & | backslash and ~ complement, as fact{*} & ~[draft], then keep (selection-algebra.ts:25, selection-algebra.ts:58, mode-mapfilter.ts:222)`
  search = `exists: like this finds lines of the same shape and names how the nearest differ (map-like.ts:40)`
  escape = `a JavaScript map and filter run through new Function in an editor beside the Spw forms (mode-mapfilter.ts:72, mode-mapfilter.ts:268)`
  fold = `absent: the host offers map and filter, in Spw and in its JavaScript editors, but no fold; a candidate is ^ over a selection, since ^ lifts parts into one relation (operators.ts) and liftPending already writes a gather into a body (link-confirm.ts:131)`
  engineer_answer = `today one can map, filter and search lines and see each hit lit before it lands; one cannot compute a value, recurse or fold`
}
?["which carries memory and timing in factshift: the canvas's physics, a sheet, or a kept register bank"]{
  ~#readings: [
    `one keeps the field honest to today's host and costs nothing to parse, but computes nothing`,
    `two answers the engineer with values and a dependency order, at the price of a bundle cut and an @ collision`,
    `three makes $ a real memory reader and gives combinations a runtime home, but waits on the runtime environment gap`
  ]
}

# ── The workbench's field theory against its runtime, by an agent reading this repo ─

#>field_model_report
#:status #!proposed
~#measured: "14 November 2026 at 1f87112f, by inline tsx runs that wrote no file"
^"theory_vs_code"{
  memory = .{
    theory = `a register bank with a default register, history 0 to 9 and named a to z, where ? raises liminality, ^ lowers it, & couples and * deepens measure (register-bank.spw:33 to 45); a hot cache of open holes and a warm one of field snapshots per beat (field-dynamics.spw:74 to 81)`
    code = `RegisterBank maps a key to a value and meta (provenance capped at 16, lenses, valence, liminality, frequency, coupling, measureDepth; register-bank.ts:276 to 354, 726 to 731); eviction scores age, cost, liminality and coupling (memory-policy.ts:88 to 131); HotRuntimeSession keeps two BeatCache planes keyed by channel, dialect and content hash (hot-session.ts:153 to 219) with TTLs of 8, 64 and 256 beats (memory-cache.ts:43 to 47)`
    gap = `no environment: ONF puts the word of *x{5} in frames.label and the interpreter reads frames.value (interpreter.ts:48 to 54, 155 to 157), so *x{5} writes the focus register, =total[3] writes a register named 3, and 5 arrives as the string 5; no operator moves liminality, only liminality-bridge.ts:123 does`
  }
  expression = .{
    theory = `operators as actors with per-sigil strategies, ~ lazy to a thunk, ? interactive to a stream head, $ introspecting substrate, all marked proposed (operators.spw:144 to 160)`
    code = `interpretSeed normalizes to ONF and evaluates every argument eagerly before dispatch (interpreter.ts:160, 377 to 381); the quantity sheet is the one evaluator with references and re-reads bracket text with its own tokenizer (sheet.ts:80 to 119, 232 to 244)`
    gap = `ONF drops what evaluation needs: #[1, 2, 3] keeps value 1 and armCount 3 and loses 2 and 3, %total[@a + @b] keeps no argument, ?[_]{ 1 } loses its frame and yields true; the AST keeps all of it (Binding, Match, Spread, Wildcard, Frame.content, Expression.connectors; nodes.ts:44 to 120, 239 to 253), so an evaluator walks the AST`
  }
  consequence = .{
    theory = `!{ } ~<consequence> is a discharge beside a potential membrane (composition-forms.spw:38 to 44); discharge is a collapse or measure write under a channel ceiling (brace-charge-crawl.spw:329 to 335, operational-field.spw:55 to 59)`
    code = `composition-eval.ts:155 to 179 recognizes the form and returns finding strings with ok true, running nothing; writes emit write, couple, phase-advance and mark events to a Substrate (substrate.ts:22, 104 to 130); effectCeiling runs none to l2 by channel (channels.ts:67 to 124) and collapse refuses under none (hot-session.ts:527 to 534)`
    gap = `no package calls Substrate.bind, so a consequence is a log line nobody handles; the log is read only whole (stages.ts:158, resonance.ts:22, probe-measure.ts:106), and influence is guessed by finding one key name inside another key's written value (resonance.ts:153 to 170), not recorded as a read`
  }
  potential = .{
    theory = `~ primes without writing and ? primes epistemically (brace-charge-crawl.spw:170 to 190); charge is latent, potentiated, bound, mobile, discharged or shielded (brace-charge-crawl.spw:130 to 137); _ is the point with no path and the hole reused for an optional root (reference-deref-geometry.spw:230 to 234, 386 to 390); $slot is a template hole (inline-composites.spw:109); an open wonder writes its answer set as $%[a, b, c] (wonder-field.spw:46)`
    code = `~ wraps an argument already evaluated and nothing forces it (interpreter.ts:293 to 295); _ yields null; ChargeState is typed (charge.ts:17 to 23) but applyCrawlVerbToState reaches its target from any state (crawl.ts:89 to 97), and evaluation never makes a ChargePacket`
    gap = `five names and no representation a later step can discharge: no thunk, no hole a value fills, no open question holding its answer set as data`
  }
  field = .{
    theory = `site, field as site to amplitude, carrier, coupling, decay by half life, flux as permeability times gradient, beat as decay then diffuse then inject, membrane as boundary law (field-dynamics.spw:28 to 41); path refs as sites and act events as injections are proposed (field-dynamics.spw:22); EM stays a profile and a solver is refused (em-fixity-association.spw:257 to 275)`
    code = `field.ts implements each primitive with conservation tests (field.ts:56 to 139, 250 to 276), and no runtime, CLI or extension module calls one; only exports and two catalogs naming it as a machine refer to it (formula-scan.ts:79 to 93, idioms.ts:70 to 78)`
    gap = `a solver with no sites: nothing maps a cell, a reference or a container to a site, and field_order already says nothing measured is conserved, signed or additive (interpretation-trials.spw:945)`
  }
  probes = .{
    match = `?match[@n]{ 0 => 1 _ => 2 } parses to a Match node, ONF keeps its arms (normalize.ts:544), and the runtime returns 1 by running it as a plain ?`
    comparison = `?[n < 2] and ?[a == b] degrade to prose though == lexes as COMPARISON (punctuation.ts:99 to 104) and Condition is typed (nodes.ts:336 to 340); no grammar makes one`
    postfix = `substrate$, x!, data~ and { a }! each parse as two statements; no Operation.position is stamped`
  }
}
^"readings"{
  one = .{
    name = `total_dataflow: the sheet's rule made general`
    cell = `a binding @name: expr is a cell holding value, inputs (names it read), span (its AST node), valence (the expression's modifier chain), state (open, ready or failed) and the beat it was computed at; RegisterMeta carries provenance and valence, and PhaseEnvelope.lineage (types.ts:148) is already a slot for inputs`
    evaluate = `walk the AST: Binding defines, a Reference in an expression reads and records an input, a number Literal is a number, # with a frame is a finite set, connectors fold left as ONF already folds them, ?match picks an arm by shape, a body whose match input is _ is a function and / applies it; any order, a cycle refused as sheet.ts:256 to 260 refuses one`
    propagate = `a write marks its dependents and recomputes them in topological order; each recompute emits a write event with its inputs, so the substrate log becomes a dependency trace instead of a text guess`
    potential = `_ is an open cell and a cell reading an open cell is open, as a failed sheet term fails downstream; recursion only by structure on a finite set, a spread pattern shrinking it, so every program ends; ~ marks a cell computed only when read`
    render = `sources are cells with no inputs; influence is an input edge weighted by reads per run (unsigned, not conserved, additive over runs); distance is hops along input edges from a chosen cell (a metric, not a flow); decay is beats since last compute through decayField and halfLifeToRate (field.ts:56 to 67), positive, not conserved, adding when two writes inject one site (field.ts:265 to 269)`
    costs = `no general recursion until a minus sign and a comparison exist; a binding and a measure frame become two ways to define a cell while the sheet keeps its own reader`
  }
  two = .{
    name = `records_and_references, as Jsonnet and Nix`
    cell = `the file is a lazy record; a field holds a thunk until forced, then a value with its forcing chain as provenance; _ is a parameter and every unforced field is potential`
    propagate = `none by default: a change makes a new record and a host diffs two forced records`
    render = `the demand trace: which field forced which, in order, with depth; unforced fields drawn faint`
    costs = `programs may not end, so a hover needs a fuel limit; the picture shows what was asked, not what is written`
  }
  three = .{
    name = `effects: operators as requests a host handles`
    cell = `reading one plus a queue of pending requests (!draw, ~spin, ?ask), each with its target address and the ceiling it needs; an operator whose meaning is the host's emits a request and continues with a placeholder`
    propagate = `requests reach Substrate.bind handlers by key or kind (substrate.ts:136 to 140), which nothing binds today; under effectCeiling none they queue and never discharge, and ChargeState gets enforced steps: potentiated when queued, discharged when answered, shielded when refused`
    render = `the queue: what is asked of whom, what waits, what the channel holds back`
    costs = `two hosts may answer one request differently, so a file's meaning depends on its host; a layer over one, not a model alone`
  }
  left = `readers_only is today; rewriting stays a file tool and would draw as a trail of rewrites, not a field`
}
^"marks_in_the_model"{
  dollar = `$ makes an address, not a value: $name is a handle to the cell name that a host can pin and follow, meta reachable and value unread; this keeps $ as select and address (reference-deref-geometry.spw:106) and $slot as a named hole (inline-composites.spw:109), since an address to a cell with no value yet is that hole`
  percent = `% defines or reads a measured cell: %term[expr] is a cell whose expression has a kind, %name the cell's measure; today two meanings disagree, the sheet's quantity with a dimension and the runtime's magnitude clamped to 0 to 1 (register-bank.ts:515 to 523, register-bank.spw:53)`
  hash = `# builds the finite set a fold walks and names a lens: #[1, 2, 3] is a value, #name[ ] puts members under a lens, and a lens is a region a host draws a boundary round, so permeability counts input edges that cross it (interpretation-trials.spw:911 counted references out of bodies); read as coverage (wonder_trial_inside), a cell sits in two lenses at once and regions overlap`
  dollar_percent_today = `written on 1,213 lines and read by six text patterns, never from the tree (probe-measure.ts:73, flow-protocol.ts:168, display.ts:607, semantic-tokens.ts:179, spw-probes.ts:269, wonder.ts:219); the parser reads $ then %[ ] as two statements and the runtime then makes a register named for the first member`
  prefix_vs_postfix = .{
    dollar_word = `$substrate, one Operation today: the address of the cell substrate, pointed before it is inhabited; it reads nothing, so it is safe under effectCeiling none`
    word_dollar = `substrate$, two statements today: inhabit then address, the cell computed and $ handing over its value with provenance; subject$ item already captures item as a modifier, the slot valence chains ride, so a postfix $ before a word collides with valence`
    dollar_measure = `$%[subject.item]: the address of the measures declared on subject.item, a query that reads no value`
    dollar_set = `$#[subject.item]: the address of its members as a nominal set with no scale, closer to a wonder's answer partition than %, which promises a scale the answers lack; written on no line`
    frame_postfix = `[subject.item]%$ and [subject.item]#$, three statements today: subject first, measure or gather it, then hand over the result with provenance, the consequence side of the same address`
    law = `prefix points and reads nothing; postfix follows, so it is an input edge and may need a ceiling; the pair is the point arm and follow arm the theory keeps visibly apart (reference-deref-geometry.spw:287 to 295)`
  }
}
^"combinatorics"{
  grounds = .{
    bank_today = `each mark already has one memory act: * and = write with force, # writes and indexes a lens, & merges into a key, @ writes the observe register, $ reads meta, % reads and deepens measure, . reads a path, <> adds an edge, and !, ^, ~ and ? write nothing (interpreter.ts:202 to 316); timing is always now, since arguments evaluate before dispatch (interpreter.ts:160)`
    lattice = `particles.ts:1 to 13 already composes three positions, a stance before #, the # plane, and an aim after it (> points, : classifies, ! asserts), with ~# aspect kept apart and ## unoccupied; a run of marks can borrow that order`
    today = `every run splits: ~*x is ~ then *x, $%x is $ then %x, and #$x is one # whose line payload is the text $x; runs such as ~*, *~, !~ and ~= sit on 7 lines here; operator token spans still tell ~*x (touching) from ~ *x (spaced), so a reader sees a run without a grammar change`
  }
  per_mark = .{
    tilde = `memory: held unwritten and forgotten unless kept, a prime that bleeds away (wonder_trial_ephemeral_bias); timing: deferred until read or kept`
    star = `memory: commit, a write that seals; timing: now`
    equals = `memory: a setting that stands until rewritten; timing: now, then on change for whoever reads it`
    at = `memory: a read by position, an input edge; timing: on change, since a read subscribes`
    dollar = `memory: an address with no read; timing: none, an address does not age`
    percent = `memory: a read that counts (measureDepth); timing: sampled, each beat when tied to the session clock`
    dot = `memory: retain, the ground a reset returns to (wonder_trial_rest_state); timing: at rest`
    hash = `memory: index under a lens, a scope a host draws; timing: each beat, as vibration is an observed write rate (register-bank.ts:778 to 800)`
    amp = `memory: many writes merged into one; timing: on change of any input`
    caret = `memory: lifted to the enclosing scope, a longer lifetime; timing: when the enclosing body completes`
    bang = `memory: discharged to a host and consumed; timing: now, under the channel ceiling`
    query = `memory: left open with its answer set; timing: until answered`
    until_and_scheduled = `until is no single mark but a concept, scene or ~# stance on the line (wonder_trial_until), and scheduled is already the separators ; and || (nodes.ts:96 to 101), so the mark set need not grow for either`
  }
  compose = .{
    nearest = `nearest mark binds tightest and a run reads as composition right to left, ~*x as ~(*(x)); operators.spw:171 and em-fixity-association.spw:112 already read data~! as !(~(data))`
    lattice = `a run is at most a stance and an act, as a particle is: the outer mark says when, the inner one what happens to memory; three marks or more refused`
    bundle = `a run is a set of effects and order is style; refused wherever two effects do not commute, as below`
  }
  order_matters = .{
    defer_commit = `~*x defers a commit: nothing is written until the first read, which computes x once and keeps it, a lazy memoized cell; *~x commits a deferral: the register holds a promise now and a host sees a pending cell; checkable as writes before the first read, 0 against 1`
    prime_act = `!~x actualizes what was primed and ~!x primes an act without firing it (wonder_trial_prime_actualize); today !~x comes back still wrapped (interpretation-trials.spw:298)`
    lean = `~=lean holds a bias as potential, gone unless kept; =~lean writes a standing setting whose value is pending (wonder_trial_ephemeral_bias)`
    measure_address = `$%x is the address of a measurement point on x with its value unread (form-ladders.ts:499 and 517 name $%[m] so); %$x measures the cell's memory, not its value: writes, age, frequency, coupling; one hands back a handle, the other a number`
    set_address = `$#x is the address of a lens over x; #$x is a set of addresses, a scope listing cells; # followed by text is a heading line today, so #$x cannot be written as a run until that rule yields`
    commuting = `two reads commute ($. and .$ name one address); a read and a write do not, nor a defer and any memory act; a turn written as a line (wonder_trial_turn) is undone by reversing its run, which only works if this table is law`
  }
}
^"smallest_slice"{
  program = [`@sum: ?match[_]{ [] => 0, [@h, ...@t] => @t / @sum + @h }`, `@total: #[1, 2, 3] / @sum`]
  parses_today = `both lines parse with no error or warning; ONF folds the arm as (t through sum) plus h, the left fold the walk uses, so no precedence choice is needed; written @h + @t / @sum it folds as (h plus t) through sum and would be wrong`
  runs_today = `runSpw returns two observe frames with null values and makes a register named 1`
  measured = `an inline AST walk of about 45 lines returned total 6 with four applications at depth 0, 1, 2 and 3 and ten reads`
  files = .{
    cells = `packages/spw-runtime/src/evaluator/cells.ts, about 110 lines: Cell, CellTable, define, read with input recording, topological recompute, cycle refusal after sheet.ts:250 to 272`
    walk = `packages/spw-runtime/src/evaluator/evaluate-ast.ts, about 180 lines: Binding, Reference, number Literal, # frame, connectors + and / only, Match with empty, spread and wildcard arms, _ as the input; any other node is reported unsupported, never guessed`
    view = `packages/spw-runtime/src/evaluator/field-view.ts, about 80 lines: spw.field-view/1 with sites (cell, span, value, state), edges (from, to, reads), depth per application and decayed amplitude per beat through decayField`
    tests = `packages/spw-runtime/src/evaluator/evaluate-ast.test.ts, about 100 lines: total 6; binding order irrelevant; a two cell cycle refused; an unknown name reported; the empty set gives 0; depth equals set length; view reads equal walk reads`
    card = `a field card in packages/spw-cli, about 60 lines, printing the view as Spw; drawing stays with the canvas host, which already keeps position, heat and a home per tie`
    total = `about 530 new lines in five files; no existing file changes, and the runtime index does not export the walk until a release names it, so no bundle grows`
  }
  next_run = `the first combination after the fold is ~*x against *~x, read from operator token spans, tested by writes before first read`
  must_not_break = .{
    runtime = `interpretSeed and runSpw unchanged with the runtime's 137 tests; the walk is its own entry, not a mode of runSpw`
    release = `the spw.parser-release/2 contract: workbench runSpw of !["hello"] succeeds and createHotSession exists (build-parser-release.test.ts:355 to 377); the published day 2026.11.13 never changes`
    parser = `no grammar and no ONF change: the slice accepts only forms that parse today with no warning`
    readers = `the sheet keeps %term[expr] (sheet.ts:243 to 244), the six $%[ ] text readers keep their input, and lint:spw keeps 1,385 files passing`
  }
  leaves_out = `a minus sign, a comparison, general recursion, and $, % and # beyond the set literal; those wait on wonder_trial_comparison, wonder_trial_math_scope and wonder_trial_pipe`
}
?["Is potential one state with three sources (~ deferred, _ open, ? unanswered), or three things a host draws apart?"]{ ~#readings: ["one state: open, ready, failed, as a sheet term", "three: a thunk, a hole, an answer set", "the charge lifecycle made law: latent, potentiated, discharged, shielded"] }
?["Does $name hand over an address a host pins, or the cell's meta as the runtime does today?"]{ ~#readings: ["address: a handle, value unread", "meta: materialize as today", "both: address by prefix, meta by postfix"] }
?["Is a wonder's outcome set a measure or a set?"]{ ~#readings: ["keep $%[ ] as written on 1,213 lines", "$#[ ] as the partition and $%[ ] as its instruments", "a tree reading for $%[ ] first, so six text readers become one"] }
?["How does a run of marks compose?"]{ ~#readings: ["nearest binds tightest, read as composition", "a stance and an act, as a particle", "a bundle, refused where effects do not commute"] }
?["Is the field a picture of the dependency graph or a quantity that moves on beats?"]{ ~#readings: ["picture: edges and hops per run", "quantity: amplitude injected at a write and decayed per beat", "both, with only the quantity stamped as measured"] }


# ── A second model's review of the published page and the pair matrix ─

#>second_review_2026_11_14
^["second_review"]{
 asked: "the owner asked grok and agy to review the page Is Spw a Programming Language? and to consider the act chain matrix, under the constraint that two operators are never read as one"
 grok: "did not run: its API answered 402 Payment Required, Grok Build usage balance exhausted"
 agy: "a Gemini model through Antigravity, print mode, plan mode, sandboxed, in an empty directory; it was sent the page as text, the generated matrix, and the owner's constraints, and read nothing else"
 wrong: "it said ?match parses as prose because ? before a mark does; ?match is ? before a word and parses with no error or warning, as does the arrow in its arms"
 held: ["the engine rows overclaimed: settings lower to WGSL parameters but no loop or kernel can be written, and round-trip writers are not an evaluator", "Laws of Form is a Boolean calculus, not general computation", "the fused pairs section endorsed compound readings the owner has set aside", "the comparisons are fused by a separate matcher, so they are absent from the matrix's fused list", "three What runs rows gave no cause"]
 applied: "the page's version 2 corrects each of these; act-chains.spw takes its strains as open questions: a run between two operands (pivot, pipeline), a mark acting twice, and marks that read as relations between two sides"
 text: `
Task 1: Review of "Is Spw a Programming Language?"

Wrong or contradictory:
- The page claims Spw's syntax "mostly parses already" and cites "@sum: ?match[_]{...}" as parsing today. Yet the matrix shows ?-prefixed forms (?Xname, ?X[x]) parse as prose (P), and => triggers warnings (W). Stress tests say < turns lines into prose (though < is outside the 12-mark matrix), and $%[x] relies on literal text search.
- "Pairs read from their parts" violates the two-marks-never-one-operator rule, cites ==, !=, <=, >= absent from fused_by_the_lexer (with == and != triggering W), and stretches .. (ground+ground as range) and || (alternative+alternative as parallel).
- "What runs" says #[1, 2, 3] returns "nothing" yet "keeps only the first member," and shows =total[3] naming register 3 and ?[true]{ yes } returning true without explaining why.

Overclaimed:
- Claiming an evaluator takes ~530 lines, and rating Mandelbrot/ray tracer "strong" (WGSL settings are not numeric loops), self-description "strong" (round-trip writers are not a Lisp/JSON evaluator), and spreadsheets "works" overstates readiness.
- Spencer-Brown's Laws of Form is propositional, not general computation, and the page concedes Spw does not parse it that way.
- "72% English" mixes prose, comments, and strings without proving config lines generalize.

Unclear, missing, and first pushback:
- Missing operational semantics: lexical scope, closures, calling conventions, evaluation order, error handling, side-effect boundaries, and arithmetic (-, *, /, modulo).
- Engineers push back first on "mostly parses already" and "~530 lines" when 0/1,008 pairs chain, marks turn to prose or vanish, and standard operators (%, <, -, !=, <=) collide.

Task 2: Matrix, Desired Parsing, Fused Tokens, and Infix Runs

Desired parser output per position (when dialect allows chaining):
- XYname and XY[x]: one chained form (C) X(Y(operand)); Y binds nearest and acts first before evaluation.
- nameXY and [x]XY: one chained form (C) Y(X(operand)); X acts first on the result, then Y.
- nameXY next: nameXY finishes as Y(X(name)) separate from next; whitespace closes the postfix arm so Y never captures next.
- X[x]Y: one combined form (C) applying pre-evaluation X and post-evaluation Y to [x] under explicit dialect precedence.
- leftXYright: deterministic split or composition (see below), never silent absorption.

Defects in today's matrix classes:
- A (@~, @.): silently drops marks.
- P (?, # prefixes): swallows code as prose.
- M (114 cells in nameXY next): Y steals next.
- K (#!) and F (..): illegal operator fusion.
- B (.. prefix): misparses marks as bullets.
- J (^@, =@): ad-hoc cases instead of arm composition.
- W, E (!=, ==, ~., ~#): position-inconsistent warnings/errors.
- S (split): defect whenever a dialect permits single-operand chaining.

Fused tokens (#>, #:, #!, ~#, .., ->, ~>, ||, ==, !=, <=, >=):
- Never fuse in the lexer; emit separate marks and compose sequentially: #! (lens of act), ~# (potential lens), #> (lens toward), #: (lens binding), ~> (potential toward), .. (ground of ground), || (alternative of alternative).
- ==, !=, <=, >= remain separate marks. Because < means receives and > means points toward, numeric comparisons cannot overload <= or >= and need distinct syntax. (-> uses -, absent from the 12 marks and 6 relations.)

What a run between two operands (left...right) should mean:
- Unspaced leftXYright is ambiguous between left's postfix arm and right's prefix arm. Dialects must require whitespace between arms (leftX Yright), pivot on a relational/binary mark inside the run, or evaluate left-to-right as a pipeline.

Task 3: Three Pairs Whose Order Matters Most

1. ~ (potential) and * (crystallize):
   Prefix: ~*x memoizes x once resolved while deferring it; *~x commits the unresolved promise.
   Postfix: x~* defers x's result then commits it; x*~ commits x's result then reopens it as potential.
2. $ (substrate/address) and # (lens/set):
   Prefix: $#[x] addresses the set [x] before reading members; #$[x] lenses/indexes [x]'s address.
   Postfix: [x]$# hands over [x]'s result with its address, then gathers a set; [x]#$ gathers a set, then hands it over.
3. @ (perspective/read) and = (choose/set):
   Prefix: @=x sets x then reads that setting; =@x reads x then sets from that perspective.
   Postfix: x@= reads x's result then sets it; x=@ sets x's result then reads it.

Task 4: The Single Predictive Rule and Where It Strains

Rule: Every mark is a unary transformer applied inside-out by proximity to its operand: prefix marks act before evaluation nearest-first outward; postfix marks act on the result nearest-first outward.

Where it strains:
- Prefix-vs-postfix precedence (X[x]Y): proximity cannot decide whether X wraps ([x]Y) ($[x]#: address of what x gathers once read) or Y wraps (X[x]) (#[x]$: set evaluated, then handed over).
- Unspaced runs between operands (leftXYright): distance alone cannot partition left's postfix arm from right's prefix arm.
- Multi-argument marks (=, &, ., ^) naturally take two sides or delimiters, not pure unary wrapping.
- Repeated pairs (.., **, ~~, ==): back-to-back identical acts lack clear distinct meanings.
- Math/comparisons: overloading %, *, !, =, <, > leaves modulo, multiplication, and inequalities unspellable.
`
}
